======================================================================================
6. THE DEGENERACY PATH THAT REPORTS READY WITH Q = 0
======================================================================================

  the atomic has_statmech shortcut (rmgpy/species.py:528)
  -------------------------------------------------------
      for a 1-atom molecule it checks ONLY conformer.E0 --
      not modes, not spin_multiplicity.

      spin_multiplicity   = 0   (Arkane structure-only default)
      has_statmech()      = True   <-- reported READY
      T=298.15   Q = 0.0000   conformer S = -inf
      T=1000.00  Q = 0.0000   conformer S = -inf

  the three counts that coexist, and what each one drives
  -------------------------------------------------------
      thermo S298 carries g = 5 (the entry's R*ln(5) term)
      spin_multiplicity=1 -> Q(298.15) = 1.0000
      spin_multiplicity=3 -> Q(298.15) = 3.0000
      spin_multiplicity=5 -> Q(298.15) = 5.0000

      Q is LINEAR in spin_multiplicity, so a TST rate built from the conformer
      scales by 5/1 = 5x or 5/3 ~ 1.667x against the g the thermo actually asserts,
      while the library entropy does not move at all.
